# The baseline is a review artifact. `src/baseline.ts` writes one entry per
# line, sorted, so that a diff moves one line when one acceptance changes —
# and a reviewer can see which `reason`, `acceptedBy` or `expires` was edited.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, so without this the file
# is checked out as CRLF and rewritten as LF by the next `--update-baseline`.
# Every line changes, and a pull request that adds one acceptance becomes
# indistinguishable from one that quietly rewrote twenty.
.zero-shelter/*.json text eol=lf
.zero-shelter/*.jsonl text eol=lf

# Pinned inputs to the benchmark. A line-ending flip changes the bytes without
# changing the content, which is the same problem one layer down: `bench/README.md`
# pins these by commit precisely so a re-run compares against what was captured.
bench/captures/**/*.json text eol=lf

# Fixtures are compared byte for byte in places, and the tests assert fixed
# hash values across three operating systems.
test/fixtures/**/*.json text eol=lf
